                    },
                    "message": "but you are using the keyword and values from vpd  and the interface constants are in constants.hpp not in the dbusUtility file"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/utility/dbus_utility.hpp",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "Why do we need all the entries in this map? We need to update common interface irrespective of any condition.\nSo this map should have thing only which are not covered via common interface?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/utility/dbus_utility.hpp",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "priyaram",
                        "email": "priyangaramasamy2@gmail.com",
                        "username": "PriyangaRamasamy"
                    },
                    "message": "common interface in JSON - refers to the interfaces which are common across all FRUs.\n\nHere I don't need common interface,  I need to find the pairs of d-bus interface and property which holds the same values.\n\nNot all pairs has to be in common interface section in json."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/utility/dbus_utility.hpp",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "Most of the pairs here are in the list because they are published under common interface which is again because it is under the CI tag in JSON. \n\nIf that segment of JSON is modified, this list here needs to be updated. Implies some part of this list mimics the entry from JSON.\n\nSo, IMO why to have multiple source of same data, will have to maintain both of them in case of any change.\nThis map should only have entries which are not there in the JSON, rest should be taken care with update of CI during write if applicable.\n\n\nAlso, I agree with @jinu.joy.thomas@in.ibm.com. This is a utility file, why should this have such map.\n-> Either have it in constants\n-> or local to the cpp file which uses it."
                },
                {
